window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-7d04f9ab1f4a3eeb"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"workspace-model-availability\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">工作区模型可用性</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>用户能使用哪些模型，取决于产品界面和登录方式。在 ChatGPT 工作区中设置的模型，不会自动应用到 ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Codex、Codex CLI、IDE 扩展、Codex Cloud 或 OpenAI API。</p> <p>完整的管理方式请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"identify-the-model-boundary\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">确认模型权限边界</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>产品或身份验证边界</th> <th>模型访问权限取决于</th> <th>当前参考来源</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>ChatGPT 工作区</td> <td>工作区套餐、成员访问权限、工作区设置和受支持的角色权限</td> <td><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11165333-chatgpt-enterprise-models-limits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Enterprise 和 Edu 的模型与限额（需联网）</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>使用 ChatGPT 登录的 ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Codex、Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展</td> <td>特定客户端支持的模型，以及已登录 ChatGPT 账户具有的访问权限</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">Codex 模型</a>和当前工作区指引</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex Cloud</td> <td>托管式 Codex 工作流支持的模型，以及已登录 ChatGPT 账户具有的访问权限</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">Codex 模型</a>和 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex Cloud</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>使用 API 密钥身份验证的 ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Codex、Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展</td> <td>与该密钥关联的 OpenAI API 组织和项目</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">身份验证</a>和 <a href=\"https://platform.openai.com/docs/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI API 平台（需联网）</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>请针对用户实际使用的产品界面，查看当前信息来源。不要直接照搬其他产品的模型目录，也不要假设 ChatGPT 模型选择器中的设置会对 ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Codex、Codex CLI、IDE 扩展、Codex Cloud 和 API 平台产生相同影响。</p> <p><a id=\"set-a-clear-starting-experience-for-employees\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">为员工设置明确的初始使用体验</h2> <p>授予访问权限之前，请先配置工作区的 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Models settings（需联网）</a>。工作区所有者和管理员可以分别为 Chat 与 Work 和 Codex 配置默认初始设置。在受支持的界面中，可以为 Chat、Work 和本地 Codex 选择初始模型、推理级别、速度和新对话行为。</p> <p>这些选择是默认值，不是权限。可用模型仍取决于成员席位、角色、工作区或 API 身份、强制执行的工作区要求，以及用户正在使用的具体界面。设置初始默认值不会为用户授予不可用模型的访问权限，也不会覆盖这些要求。Codex Cloud 不支持更改默认模型。</p> <p>Fast 模式是否可用，取决于工作区、产品界面以及是否强制设置了 <code>features.fast_mode</code>。该设置位于 <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713?anchor=requirementstoml\"><code>requirements.toml</code></a> 中。它可以为受管理的本地 Codex 客户端固定启用或关闭 Fast 模式；它不是初始默认值，也不能覆盖工作区或产品可用性限制。</p> <p><a id=\"save-preview-and-launch-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"preview-launch\">保存 Preview 与 Launch 的访问权限</h2> <p>如果页面显示了可分别编辑的 Preview 和 Launch 访问权限，请选择 <strong>Save changes</strong>（保存更改）来保存设置。</p> <p>如果页面提供且允许编辑 <strong>Sync preview and launch access</strong>（同步 Preview 与 Launch 访问权限），可将其打开，以便保存时把 Preview 的选择复制到 Launch。同步只会在保存时运行，不会持续更新 Launch。关闭可选同步并保存后，Launch 会保留最近一次保存的选择，除非你同时编辑了这些选择。关闭同步时，也可以单独编辑并保存 Launch 的选择。</p> <p>成功保存后，请重新打开访问权限设置，核对已保存的选择。如果页面提示无法保存所有更改，其中一部分可能已经保存。请按照页面提示检查并保存剩余更改。</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-6-sol-and-luna-in-enterprise\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"enterprise-gpt-6-sol-luna\">在 Enterprise 中启用 GPT-6 Sol 和 Luna</h2> <p>推出时，Enterprise 工作区默认关闭 GPT-6 Sol 和 GPT-6 Luna。管理员必须先启用相应模型，成员才能选择。请检查<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区模型设置（需联网）</a>，并在每个客户端上确认访问权限。在本地配置中选择某个模型，不会覆盖工作区控制项。</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-61-sol-in-enterprise\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"enterprise-gpt-61-sol\">在 Enterprise 中启用 GPT-6.1 Sol</h2> <p>GPT-6.1 Sol 有独立的计划推出安排。在 Enterprise 和 Edu 中，管理员启用之前，此模型默认关闭。 更改工作区默认模型之前，请检查<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区模型设置（需联网）</a>和 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">Codex 模型推出说明</a>。在本地配置中选择某个模型不会授予访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-6-astra-in-enterprise\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"enterprise-gpt-6-astra\">在 Enterprise 中启用 GPT-6 Astra</h2> <p>在符合条件的 ChatGPT Enterprise 和 Edu 工作区中，Astra 首次推出时默认关闭。工作区所有者必须通过工作区模型设置启用访问权限。两周后访问权限不会自动开启。现有 Early Model Access 设置不会授予 Astra 的访问权限。 工作区所有者可以在 Chat、Work 和 Codex 中，为整个工作区或特定角色启用 Astra。现有产品资格条件仍然适用。请检查<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区模型设置（需联网）</a>，并在用户依赖的每个客户端上确认可用性。</p> <p>启用模型访问权限与选择初始模型是两项独立决定。将 Astra 设为默认模型之前，请确认适用的席位、角色和计费安排。额度和计费指引请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">价格</a>；有关因等待审核而暂停的任务，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=safety-monitoring-and-paused-tasks\">安全监控</a>。</p> <p>如果使用 API 密钥登录，Astra 的访问权限取决于与该密钥关联的 API 组织和项目。在 ChatGPT 工作区中启用 Astra 不会授予 API 访问权限。使用 API 密钥获取早期访问权限还需要配置客户端；请向 OpenAI 客户团队索取设置说明。仅选择模型或修改本地配置本身不会授予访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-for-the-gpt-55-retirement\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"gpt-55\">为 GPT-5.5 退役做好准备</h2> <p>使用 ChatGPT 登录的 Codex 将于 2026 年 10 月 14 日中午（PDT；UTC 时间 19:00）停止提供 GPT-5.5。OpenAI API 和使用 API 密钥进行身份验证的 Codex 会话不受影响。</p> <p>请检查 Codex 工作区默认设置，并选择可用的替代模型。管理员为相关用户启用 <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>（GPT-6.1 Sol）后，可将其作为替代模型。在工作区默认设置、已保存的模型设置、托管配置、自定义智能体和定时任务中，将 <code>gpt-5.5</code> 替换掉。也请检查是否有脚本或命令明确选择了 <code>gpt-5.5</code>。</p> <p>更改默认值不会授予模型访问权限。请确认受影响的用户在每个客户端上都能使用替代模型。迁移指引请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-55-retirement\">Codex 模型</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>译者注：本页 V105 冻结源于 2026 年 10 月 17 日抓取；文中所述停用时间已过。此处忠实翻译源文，实际可用性请以官方实时状态为准。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"prepare-for-the-gpt-54-retirement\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"gpt-54\">为 GPT-5.4 退役做好准备</h2> <p>使用 ChatGPT 登录的用户已于 2026 年 8 月 31 日无法再在 Codex 中使用 GPT-5.4 和 GPT-5.4 mini。请使用受影响用户的套餐和客户端可用模型，更新任何仍在使用的工作区默认设置、已保存的模型设置、托管配置、自定义智能体和定时任务：</p> <ul> <li>如果可用，请将 <code>gpt-5.4</code> 替换为 <code>gpt-6-sol</code>（GPT-6 Sol）。</li> <li>如果可用，请将 <code>gpt-5.4-mini</code> 替换为 <code>gpt-6-luna</code>（GPT-6 Luna）。在 Enterprise 和 Edu 中，管理员必须先启用 Luna。</li> </ul> <p>OpenAI API 和使用你自己的 API 密钥进行身份验证的 Codex 不受影响。迁移详情请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=deprecated-codex-models\">Codex 模型</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"separate-access-from-runtime-permissions\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">区分模型访问权限与运行时权限</h2> <p>模型访问权限决定已通过身份验证的用户能否在受支持的界面上使用某个模型。本地权限配置文件和托管要求决定本地运行开始后智能体可以执行哪些操作，例如可以修改哪些文件、访问哪些网络目标。</p> <p>权限配置文件不能授予模型访问权限。模型访问权限也不能削弱某次运行适用的沙箱、审批策略、网络控制或来源系统权限。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-model-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">排查模型访问问题</h2> <p>如果用户无法选择预期模型：</p> <ul> <li>确认产品界面和登录方式。</li> <li>确认 ChatGPT 工作区，或 Platform API 组织和项目。</li> <li>检查该身份验证边界对应的当前访问控制项。</li> <li>检查所选本地客户端或 Codex Cloud 是否支持该模型。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"current-sources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">当前参考来源</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11165333-chatgpt-enterprise-models-limits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Enterprise 和 Edu 的模型与限额（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理工作区设置（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701-rbac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">基于角色的访问控制（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">Codex 模型</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7?anchor=feature-availability\">按套餐划分的 Codex 功能可用性</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">身份验证</a></li> </ul> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员推出指南</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">群组与账户配置</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"workspace-model-availability\">Workspace model availability</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>The models available to someone depend on the product surface and how they signed in. A model setting in your ChatGPT workspace doesn't automatically apply to Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, the IDE extension, Codex cloud, or the OpenAI API.</p> <p>For the complete administration model, see <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"identify-the-model-boundary\">Identify the model boundary</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Product or authentication boundary</th> <th>Model access follows</th> <th>Current source</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>ChatGPT workspace</td> <td>The workspace plan, member access, workspace settings, and supported role permissions</td> <td><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11165333-chatgpt-enterprise-models-limits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Enterprise and Edu models and limits (online)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, and IDE extension with ChatGPT sign-in</td> <td>Models supported by the specific client and the access available to the signed-in ChatGPT identity</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">Codex models</a> and current workspace guidance</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex cloud</td> <td>Models supported by hosted Codex workflows and the access available to the signed-in ChatGPT identity</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">Codex models</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, and IDE extension with API-key authentication</td> <td>The OpenAI API organization and project associated with the key</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">Authentication</a> and the <a href=\"https://platform.openai.com/docs/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI API Platform (online)</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Check the current source for the surface the user is actually using. Don't copy a model catalog or assume that a ChatGPT model-picker setting has the same effect for Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, IDE extension, Codex cloud, and the API Platform.</p> <h2 id=\"set-a-clear-starting-experience-for-employees\">Set a clear starting experience for employees</h2> <p>Configure <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Models settings (online)</a> for your workspace before granting access. Workspace owners and admins can configure separate starting defaults for Chat and for Work and Codex. Where supported, choose a starting model, reasoning level, speed, and new-chat behavior for Chat, Work, and local Codex surfaces.</p> <p>Treat these choices as defaults, not permissions. Available models still depend on the member's seat, role, workspace or API identity, enforced workspace requirements, and the specific surface they're using. Starting defaults don't grant access to unavailable models or override those requirements. Codex cloud doesn't support changing its default model.</p> <p>Fast mode availability depends on the workspace, product surface, and any enforced <code>features.fast_mode</code> setting in <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713?anchor=requirementstoml\"><code>requirements.toml</code></a>. This setting can pin Fast mode on or off for managed local Codex clients; it isn't a starting default and can't override workspace or product availability.</p> <h2 id=\"save-preview-and-launch-access\">Save Preview and Launch access</h2> <p>Where separate Preview and Launch access settings are visible and editable, select <strong>Save changes</strong> to save your choices.</p> <p>If <strong>Sync preview and launch access</strong> is available and editable, turn it on to copy your Preview choices to Launch when you save. Sync runs when you save; it doesn't continuously update Launch access. Turning optional Sync off and saving keeps the latest saved Launch choices unless you also edit them. You can edit and save Launch choices separately with Sync off.</p> <p>After a successful save, reopen the access settings to verify the saved choices. If the page reports that it couldn't save all changes, some changes may already be saved. Follow the on-screen guidance to review and save the remaining changes.</p> <h2 id=\"gpt-6-sol-and-luna-in-enterprise\">GPT-6 Sol and Luna in Enterprise</h2> <p>GPT-6 Sol and GPT-6 Luna are off by default in Enterprise workspaces at launch. An administrator must enable each model before members can select it. Review your <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">workspace model settings (online)</a> and confirm access on each client. Choosing a model in local configuration doesn't override workspace controls.</p> <h2 id=\"gpt-61-sol-in-enterprise\">GPT-6.1 Sol in Enterprise</h2> <p>GPT-6.1 Sol has its own planned rollout. The plan keeps it off by default in Enterprise and Edu until an administrator enables it. Check your <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">workspace model settings (online)</a> and the <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">Codex model rollout</a> before changing a workspace default. Choosing a model in local configuration doesn't grant access.</p> <h2 id=\"gpt-6-astra-in-enterprise\">GPT-6 Astra in Enterprise</h2> <p>Astra is off by default at launch in eligible ChatGPT Enterprise and Edu workspaces. A workspace owner must enable access through workspace model settings. Access does not automatically turn on after two weeks. Existing Early Model Access settings do not grant access to Astra. Workspace owners can enable Astra for the workspace or specific roles across Chat, Work, and Codex. Existing product eligibility still applies. Review your <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">workspace model settings (online)</a> and confirm availability on each client your users rely on.</p> <p>Enabling access and choosing a starting model are separate decisions. Check the applicable seat, role, and billing arrangement before setting Astra as a default. See <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">pricing</a> for allowance and billing guidance and <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=safety-monitoring-and-paused-tasks\">safety monitoring</a> for tasks that pause for review.</p> <p>For API-key sign-in, Astra access follows the API organization and project associated with the key. Enabling Astra in a ChatGPT workspace doesn't grant API access. Early access with an API key also requires client configuration; ask your OpenAI account team for setup instructions. Selecting a model or changing local configuration doesn't grant access by itself.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-for-the-gpt-55-retirement\">Prepare for the GPT-5.5 retirement</h2> <p>GPT-5.5 retires from Codex with ChatGPT sign-in on October 14, 2026, at noon PDT (19:00 UTC). The OpenAI API and Codex sessions authenticated with an API key aren't affected.</p> <p>Review Codex workspace defaults and choose an available replacement. Choose <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> (GPT-6.1 Sol) once an administrator has enabled it for the affected users. Replace <code>gpt-5.5</code> in workspace defaults, saved model settings, managed configurations, custom agents, and scheduled tasks. Check scripts and commands that explicitly select <code>gpt-5.5</code> too.</p> <p>Changing a default doesn't grant model access. Confirm that the replacement is available to the affected users on each client. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-55-retirement\">Codex models</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">managed configuration</a> for migration guidance.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-for-the-gpt-54-retirement\">Prepare for the GPT-5.4 retirement</h2> <p>GPT-5.4 and GPT-5.4 mini retired from Codex for users signed in with ChatGPT on August 31, 2026. Update any remaining workspace defaults, saved model settings, managed configurations, custom agents, and scheduled tasks with models available to the affected users' plans and clients:</p> <ul> <li>Replace <code>gpt-5.4</code> with <code>gpt-6-sol</code> (GPT-6 Sol) when available.</li> <li>Replace <code>gpt-5.4-mini</code> with <code>gpt-6-luna</code> (GPT-6 Luna) when available. In Enterprise and Edu, an administrator must enable Luna first.</li> </ul> <p>The OpenAI API and Codex authenticated with your own API key aren't affected. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=deprecated-codex-models\">Codex models</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">managed configuration</a> for migration details.</p> <h2 id=\"separate-access-from-runtime-permissions\">Separate access from runtime permissions</h2> <p>Model access determines whether a model is available to the authenticated user on a supported surface. Local permission profiles and managed requirements determine what an agent can do after a local run starts, such as which files it can change or which network destinations it can reach.</p> <p>A permission profile can't grant model access. Model access also can't weaken the sandbox, approval policy, network controls, or source-system permissions that apply to a run.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshoot-model-access\">Troubleshoot model access</h2> <p>If a user can't select an expected model:</p> <ul> <li>Confirm the product surface and sign-in method.</li> <li>Confirm the ChatGPT workspace or Platform API organization and project.</li> <li>Review the current access controls for that authentication boundary.</li> <li>Check whether the selected local client or Codex cloud supports the model.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"current-sources\">Current sources</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11165333-chatgpt-enterprise-models-limits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Enterprise and Edu models and limits (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage workspace settings (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701-rbac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Role-based access control (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">Codex models</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7?anchor=feature-availability\">Codex feature availability by plan</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">Authentication</a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">Groups and provisioning</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a></li> </ul>"};
